# Keep the build context to the sources under test. Anything excluded here is unavailable to CI,
# which is the point: a check that can only pass because of something on the developer's machine is
# not a check.

# History and credentials. The commit under test is passed in as LOCAL_CI_COMMIT instead.
#
# `.git` only — not `.gitignore`, which is a checked-in source file that tests assert against. An
# earlier revision excluded both and the suite failed inside the container while passing outside it,
# which is precisely the class of divergence containerising CI is supposed to remove.
.git

# Results of previous runs. Including them would let a stale record travel into a new image.
artifacts/local-ci

# Never present in this repository (no third-party dependencies), and excluded so that a stray
# local install cannot silently become part of a CI run.
node_modules

# Agent and editor state. Not part of the repository's behaviour.
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# Build context noise.
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
